message: "If you refer to the Vector Humanities site in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Vector Humanities: humanities research in and on the vector medium"
abstract: >-
  The website of Vector Humanities, a research lab directed by David M. Berry
  at the University of Sussex. It documents projects that take the vector
  medium as both the instrument and the object of humanities research: the
  Vector Lab instruments, the vector translation of Kuki Shūzō's The Problem
  of Contingency, the Vector Humanities Editions & Contingencies book series,
  the Melville Research Bench, critical code studies readings of ELIZA,
  Spacewar! and SHRDLU, and Nostos as a case of vector literature. It also
  sets out vector toolmaking and the lab's working conventions on provenance,
  AI disclosure, instrument and material, and open access.
